<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Overlay for org.cyanogenmod.platform-res.apk (the CM SDK resource package),
    device/kyocera/msm8926-common.

    Path guess: the module that produces org.cyanogenmod.platform-res.apk is
    frameworks/base/packages/CyanogenModPlatformRes in cm-14.1.  The shipped
    image does not rely on it: both bools are patched straight into the
    packaged apk's resources.arsc, four bytes each, no rebuild and no
    renumbering (tools/image/arsc_patch.py; docs/DEVICE_NOTES.md 41).

    config_proximityCheckOnWake was false, which switched off two things at
    once:

      * PhoneWindowManager never installed its proximity listener, so the
        "do not light the screen while the phone is in a pocket" check was
        dead code;
      * CM's Settings saw proximity_on_wake as unavailable and hid the
        toggle, which is the "the proximity sensor does not do anything"
        symptom.

    EnabledByDefault is turned on as well.  That is a deliberate behaviour
    change and it is safe here only because the sensor was measured working:
    dumpsys sensorservice in the fix78 dump shows SFH7776 proximity reporting
    3.00/4.00 on-change events while com.android.systemui's FalsingManager had
    it open.  If it ever has to be backed out, Settings -> Display ->
    "Prevent accidental wake-up" is the switch, no reflash needed.
-->
<resources>
    <bool name="config_proximityCheckOnWake">true</bool>
</resources>
